      "syllabusTopic": "Intercropping systems: principles, canopy architecture, and competition indices (LER, ATER, RCC, CR, Aggressivity)",
      "questionText": "Define Land Equivalent Ratio (LER) and explain how it evaluates the biological efficiency of intercropping.",
      "modelAnswer": "The **Land Equivalent Ratio (LER)** is the most widely adopted mathematical index for evaluating the biological efficiency, land-use advantage, and productivity of an intercropping system compared to sole cropping.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\\text{LER} = L_A + L_B = \\left( \\frac{Y_{AB}}{Y_{AA}} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{Y_{BA}}{Y_{BB}} \\right)$$\nWhere:\n- $Y_{AB}$ = Yield of crop A grown as an intercrop with crop B\n- $Y_{AA}$ = Yield of crop A grown as a sole crop\n- $Y_{BA}$ = Yield of crop B grown as an intercrop with crop A\n- $Y_{BB}$ = Yield of crop B grown as a sole crop\n- $L_A$ and $L_B$ = Partial LERs of species A and B, respectively.\n\n### Biological Interpretation\n- **LER > 1.0:** Demonstrates a definitive **yield advantage** and superior land-use efficiency. For example, an LER of 1.35 indicates that an intercropping system produces 35% more total yield per unit area than pure stands, meaning a farmer would require 1.35 hectares of sole cropping to produce the identical harvest obtained from 1.0 hectare of intercropping.\n- **LER = 1.0:** Indicates zero yield advantage; intercropping productivity is identical to sole cropping.\n- **LER < 1.0:** Indicates a yield disadvantage, reflecting mutual competitive inhibition where negative inter-specific competition outweighs complementary cooperation.",
      "outlinePoints": [
        "Definition of LER: relative sole crop land area required to match intercrop output",
        "Formula breakdown: LER = (Y_AB / Y_AA) + (Y_BA / Y_BB)",
        "Partial LERs (L_A and L_B) representing individual species performance",
        "Interpretation of LER > 1.0 (yield advantage / land savings)",
        "Interpretation of LER = 1.0 and LER < 1.0 (competitive inhibition)"
      ]
